---
apiVersion: v1
kind: Secret
metadata:
  name: livesync
  namespace: {{ k8s_namespace }}
type: Opaque
stringData:
  # CouchDB's admin password. It MUST match the Docker twin's: the seeded _users/_dbs shards
  # carry password hashes, and CouchDB's entrypoint only writes the admin credential into
  # local.d/docker.ini when no admin is configured yet. A different value here would leave the
  # Obsidian clients' stored basic-auth rejected against a database that is otherwise intact.
  #
  # Note what is NOT here: livesync_sync_token. That gate stays at the Docker edge, in a
  # mode-0600 file-provider config, which is the whole reason it lives there rather than on a
  # container label (traefik/config.yml.j2). A k8s Secret is base64, not encrypted, and readable
  # by anything with API access to the namespace — so moving it here would trade one metadata
  # leak for another.
  COUCHDB_PASSWORD: "{{ livesync_db_password }}"
